redges, so both stars are stored rows and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed"},{"type":"text","text":" swaps the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"planes in O(1). Every vertex-space read hashes its vertex once; index-space reads and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms hash none. Hyperedges can be appended but not removed. Equality"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignores the order of the vertices and of the hyperedges."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceList","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph stored as an incidence list: each hyperedge’s sources and targets, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex’s out- and in-hyperedges (Gallo’s forward and backward stars), as two planes of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":"’s storage. Unprefixed, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":" is the directed one of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair. ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" is the matrix form; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" is undirected, because"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“oriented incidence matrix” is the established name.)"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencelist"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceList"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs13IncidenceListV","title":"IncidenceList","role":"symbol","modules":[{"na